  "question": {
    "text": "If the expansion in powers of $x$ of the function $\\frac{1}{(1-a x)(1-b x)}$ is $a_0+a_1 x+a_2 x^2+a_3 x^3+\\ldots$, then $a_n$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zu2w6",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{b^n-a^n}{b-a}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2hdLh",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{a^n-b^n}{b-a}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UkvbC",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{a^{n+1}-b^{n+1}}{b-a}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nLKIl",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{b^{n+1}-a^{n+1}}{b-a}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$(1-a x)^{-1}(1-b x)^{-1}=\\left(1+a x+a^2 x^2+\\ldots \\ldots\\right)\\left(1+b x+b^2 x^2+\\ldots.\\right)$\n$\\therefore$ coefficient of $x^n=b^n+a b^{n-1}+a^2 b^{n-2}+\\ldots .+a^{n-1} b+a^n=\\frac{b^{n+1}-a^{n+1}}{b-a}$\n$\\therefore a_n=\\frac{b^{n+1}-a^{n+1}}{b-a}$",
    "image": null
  },
